Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Topology", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Abstract written by Pavel Hajek on 27 October 2026.", \
"TI"]], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We consider topology as viewed by an observer at scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3961a0f9-c7a4-4508-9efa-604fab068532"],
 ". The ",
 StyleBox["ball intersection complex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", computed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["BallIntersectionComplex"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/BallIntersectionComplex", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7433bb99-5fc5-4ee2-b62e-f45016c9c715"],
 ", uses the information of overlaps of cover by balls of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27968daf-7320-4780-99bc-9accd9bcee75"],
 ". A collection of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ba8f64f-3afe-47f7-958a-e8ce323b6582"],
 " balls forms a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b31ac376-db98-4138-bebb-26642a4eb7bd"],
 "-simplex when every subcollection of at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71187669-cbd3-4703-8f93-462b8143d027"],
 " balls has a common point. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d3e577ca-70dd-4cd6-a230-651736fedbb8"],
 ", we obtain the ",
 StyleBox["Cech complex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", computed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CechComplex"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/CechComplex", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "afb0b98a-0d56-49fc-b332-8d77c4e827a8"],
 ". For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cedf5e30-b3a5-4082-8b0d-244fbd8add55"],
 ", we obtain the ",
 StyleBox["Vietoris-Rips complex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " with threshold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511891b8-5684-4b9b-8f7e-8783bca65271"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We consider several notions of ",
 StyleBox["dimension",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " at an observer scale. A ",
 StyleBox["Hausdorff-type dimension",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is based on the number of balls of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "<", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f79ae4e-e590-45cb-b937-58c1597da317"],
 " needed to cover a ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52fb89e7-ac1f-4004-9122-75d1cf753686"],
 " around a point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05f5c914-cf81-4fa1-9de1-5ebdf805edbe"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["BallCoverNumber"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/BallCoverNumber", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c9a4c578-f4e2-4319-85e5-cd64e807e4f1"],
 " computes the minimal number of balls, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindBallCover"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindBallCover", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "afbb6834-bab3-440d-9117-f3a9f80c5364"],
 " finds their centers. In particular, we can study how the number of radius-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "220880fb-2653-455f-b875-6846539447fc"],
 " balls needed to cover a radius-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d0aea5e2-d9a3-45df-8c9e-537b5335e119"],
 " ball changes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "afc9620d-2ea3-4bd7-909c-3e7ad0435153"],
 ". Another notion is based on the maximal number of ",
 StyleBox["mutually orthogonal axes",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3885e3a0-ae3b-4e4d-b7cc-f7fdb1b28f68"],
 " through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "517c2f75-e70a-4985-af34-cc95e030d9e5"],
 ", computed using ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraOrthogonalAxes"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraOrthogonalAxes", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1a53d3a4-e737-4de3-8547-1145fc525e53"],
 ". We also define a dimension using ",
 StyleBox["equidistant sets",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": starting from pairs of maximally distant points on the radius-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb79cd0-3fd4-4620-827c-aff8e2b6f2d6"],
 " shell around ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6864e530-269d-4f81-9934-d2330daf6897"],
 ", we consider their perpendicular bisectors and ask for the maximal number \
of independent bisectors having a nonempty common intersection. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraEquidistantSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraEquidistantSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "56802da8-52f4-4da3-8be9-8e182b02464d"],
 " represents this common set, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraEquidistantSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraEquidistantSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2e4d3bdd-8f88-44e7-a0f4-7a6dadf9cd4d"],
 " computes it. A further notion uses intersections of radius-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8c89272-4997-4237-82fd-1220403e2a15"],
 " balls and asks for the smallest intersection order at which intersections \
of small subcollections determine whether the whole family has a common \
point. Finally, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["VolumeGrowthObservables"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/VolumeGrowthObservables", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f5ee767-de34-4ec6-9340-5b1545911387"],
 " implements the Riemannian idea of extracting dimension, together with \
scalar curvature, from the growth of ",
 StyleBox["ball and shell volumes",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " with radius."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We also study ",
 StyleBox["homotopy of paths and loops",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " through small deformations. \"NullHomotopicCycles\" specifies which cycles \
can be contracted. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraHomotopy"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraHomotopy", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1c497aef-9c03-474e-9a07-86ff8465bf01"],
 " finds deformations, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HomotopicQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/HomotopicQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ddff5718-ea8a-4ed6-a0b0-d63ebfa2b8f9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NullHomotopicQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/NullHomotopicQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "86644284-a12e-4935-8553-190242908703"],
 " test homotopy and null-homotopy. We also consider ",
 StyleBox["forward deformations of shortest paths",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": distance from the starting point never decreases, and excess length \
counts steps within distance shells. These walks can be counted using \
adjacency-matrix powers. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDeformationSize"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDeformationSize", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ecfa9542-8ad3-4ca8-a462-41ad043f50fb"],
 " measures how many edges of the reference path are replaced."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Infra topology also includes the ",
 StyleBox["topological properties of fibre bundles",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", discussed in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Infra Fiber Bundles"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/guide/InfraFiberBundles"},
   "RefLinkPlain",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b27dd528-ea9b-412b-afa5-874d5185411d"],
 " guide."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

